::'''Himeko:''' So, I figured out a way to go inside the Express. The internal structure was incredible, especially its engine...
::'''Himeko:''' By the time I came to my senses, I had already passionately finished fixing the Express and was already embarking on a journey aboard it.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} What kind of wild plot is this?
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} This is mind-control, right?
:::'''Himeko:''' Many developments in life are inherently unexpected or uncontrollable, just like your experience with the Express.

;(Talk to Welt Yang)
:{{Black Screen|You explain the results of the investigation to Welt and Himeko...}}
:'''Himeko:''' Heh... Interesting. What a surprising turn of events.
:'''Himeko:''' I knew the IPC had been on this planet before the Eternal Freeze, but as far as I was aware, it had pulled everyone out before the Antimatter Legion officially landed on Jarilo-VI.
:'''Himeko:''' I didn't think they would actually send someone to keep an eye on a planet engulfed in the Eternal Freeze... That however does sounds like their way of doing things.
:'''Welt:''' Since it's just an ad message, it shouldn't pose a threat to Jarilo-VI. Thanks to your findings, we can all rest easy after all.
:'''Welt:''' As promised, Himeko and I have prepared a reward for you.
:'''Himeko:''' ...Huh? Whose phone is ringing?
<pre>{
	"$type": "RPG.GameCore.PlayMessage",
	"MessageSectionID": 1112700
}</pre>
:'''Welt:''' History after the Eternal Freeze... Our data bank doesn't seem to have any relevant documents on this topic.
:'''Himeko:''' Looks like the go-getter on our crew, (Trailblazer), has another new mission. Good luck!
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} How can I learn about that history?
::'''Himeko:''' Hehe. That's where our Trailblaze comes in.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I really don't want to go...
::'''Himeko:''' Hehe. I knew you would say that.
::'''Welt:''' The way I see it, this is a good opportunity to enrich the Express' data bank... I assume you don't yet know everything about this planet, and you might as well take this chance to learn a bit about its history. What say you, (Trailblazer)?
::'''Himeko:''' Welt is right. As for where you should go to learn about this history...
:'''Himeko:''' If my memory still serves me well... You've connected with a young Supreme Guardian during this journey. Isn't that right?
:'''Himeko:''' She is likely the person closest to the true history of the planet. Go and ask her. You might learn something.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I'll be on my way then.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} How about giving me my rewards first?
::'''Himeko:''' Hehe. Not so quick, (Trailblazer). This investigation is now being extended, so it's not quite the time to dole out rewards just yet.
::'''Welt:''' ...Don't take advantage of (Trailblazer). But Himeko does have a point. We will give you your reward after this matter has been completely resolved.
:'''Himeko:''' Have a safe trip, (Trailblazer). I hope your journey will prove fruitful.
:{{Black Screen|You explain the results of the investigation to Welt and Himeko...}}
<pre>{
	"$type": "RPG.GameCore.SaveMessage",
	"MessageSectionID": 1112700
}</pre>
{{Dialogue End}}

===Go learn about Belobog's history from Bronya{{subst:void|<!--201150108-->}}===
{{Mission Description|type=adventure|location=Qlipoth Fort|update|The Interastral Peace Appliances salesperson hurriedly interrupts your conversation (via text message). Now, you have no choice but to accept their? ''Its?'' Request.<br />Despite your reluctance, you should listen to Himeko and head to Qlipoth Fort to ask Supreme Guardian Bronya's opinion.}}
{{Dialogue Start}}

;(Talk to Bronya)
:'''Bronya:''' Before the Eternal Freeze? I do know about it, but I can't recite it all by memory.
:'''Bronya:''' If you are really interested, you should look on the shelf over there for a set of books called ''Belobog Chronicles''. They might be helpful references.
:'''Bronya:''' What got you suddenly interested in researching that history anyway? Did something happen?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Long story. It all started with an ad...
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I'm on a research mission for the Express' data bank.
:'''Bronya:''' I see...
:'''Bronya:''' ...Oh. What was that sound?
<pre>{
	"$type": "RPG.GameCore.PlayMessage",
	"MessageSectionID": 1112800
}</pre>
:'''Bronya:''' Pfft... I totally get it now.
:'''Bronya:''' That ''Chronicle'' is on the bookshelf. Feel free to have a look. If you can't find it, just let me know. I'll help you look.
:'''Bronya:''' The name Interastral Peace Appliances... does seem to ring a bell.
:'''Bronya:''' Interastral Peace Appliances... Interastral Peace...
:'''Bronya:''' Interastral Peace Corporation... I've read about it before in the Guardians' history textbook. I think it's some kind of interstellar organization that has massive influences all over the cosmos. It has something to do with Preservation...
:'''Bronya:''' Oh... never mind. They're all followers of the Amber Lord, but they probably have nothing to do with Belobog. So I need not worry about them for now.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Not necessarily.
::'''Bronya:''' Hmmm... maybe you're right. But I still believe they might be a net positive for Belobog if there comes a time when we do make contact with them in the future.
::'''Bronya:''' Alright. Go and find the book you need. Just let me know if you need any help.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I'll go look for the records then. Thank you.
::'''Bronya:''' You're welcome. I hope Qlipoth Fort's book collection will be of use to you.
<pre>{
	"$type": "RPG.GameCore.SaveMessage",
	"MessageSectionID": 1112800
}</pre>
{{Dialogue End}}

===Look for the ''Belobog Chronicles'' in the bookcase{{subst:void|<!--201150109-->}}===
{{Mission Description|type=adventure|location=Qlipoth Fort|update|You've lost count of how many times this salesperson had interrupted you, but you eventually learn from Bronya where the information might be kept.<br />Investigate the hulking bookcase in Qlipoth Fort as per Bronya's tip.}}
{{Dialogue Start}}

{{Dialogue End}}

===Report in once again to the crew about the results of the investigation{{subst:void|<!--201150111-->}}===
{{Mission Description|type=adventure|location=Parlor Car|update|Text messages... endless darn messages &mdash; This salesperson doesn't sound like someone who's asking for help, but more like that boss they mentioned.<br />Anyways, you got the important historical records regarding Belobog's icebound years... Hopefully this'll get the salesperson off your back.<br />Oh, don't forget to fill the Crew in on all the relevant details.}}
{{Dialogue Start}}

;(Talk to Himeko)
;(If {{cx}}<!--SubMission not Finish: 101150222--> and {{cx}}<!--SubMission Finish: 101100201-->)
:;(First interaction)
:::'''Himeko:''' What's up, (Trailblazer)? Back on the Express slacking off, huh?
:::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I'm here to listen to your stories...
:::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I'm free for now and want to hear you talk about the past...
:::'''Himeko:''' Oh, I almost forgot about that... Then, to make a long story short, where should I begin?
:::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Himeko, when did you first board the Express?
::::'''Himeko:''' Now that's got me stumped...
::::'''Himeko:''' Seven years, eight years... No, that's not right. I'm sorry. I'm not Dan Heng &mdash; I've never kept a diary aboard the Express.
::::'''Himeko:''' The Express traverses through different worlds, and the flow of time can become blurry...
::::'''Himeko:''' But I'm clear about the beginning of my story with the Express. That day just so happened to be my birthday. Back then, I was hiking outdoors and looking for a place without any light pollution to observe the light and orbit of Heaven's Finger.
::::'''Himeko:''' Then, using a telescope, I saw a bright spot streak across the sky. I thought it was a comet and thought nothing of it.
::::'''Himeko:''' But it wasn't until the spot grew bigger and bigger that I realized there was something wrong... That thing pierced straight through the atmosphere without burning up, and flew straight at me.
::::'''Himeko:''' So I drove as fast as I could to get out of there, until I heard a loud crash behind me as if the entire world had been flipped upside down...
::::'''Himeko:''' I saw a train half-buried in a huge crater. When it happened, I said to myself that this cannot possibly be a thing of this world. It's too dangerous to get close to it...
::::'''Himeko:''' But, out of basic human curiosity, I dared to take a closer look. I keep thinking to myself, just one look, just one look.
::::'''Himeko:''' So, I figured out a way to go inside the Express. The internal structure was incredible, especially its engine...
::::'''Himeko:''' By the time I came to my senses, I had already passionately finished fixing the Express and was already embarking on a journey aboard it.
::::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} What kind of wild plot is this?
::::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} This is mind-control, right?
:::::'''Himeko:''' Many developments in life are inherently unexpected or uncontrollable, just like your experience with the Express.
:::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} When did you and Mr. Yang meet?
::::'''Himeko:''' About that... Um... When did Welt get here?
::::'''Himeko:''' Many years ago, Pom-Pom and I were tasked by Herta to go to the abandoned and ruined world of Salsotto, looking for a special material called Cadence Glass...
::::'''Himeko:''' Just as the Express finished its warp jump, we picked up an unknown signal. It was coming from the wreckage of a huge starship.
::::'''Himeko:''' Based on the ''Express Safety Manual'', such an obviously dangerous signal should be ignored. You have no idea whether the party sending the signal is a victim needing rescue, or a bandit lurking behind a trap...
::::'''Himeko:''' But out of basic human curiosity, we decided to take a look and immediately set out for Salsotto to do our business.
::::'''Himeko:''' Welt joined up with us after that.
::::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Wait... You're missing lots of details, aren't you?
::::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} What exactly happened?
::::'''Himeko:''' There was no torturous rescue process, just the normal procedures. In the end, there were two new passengers on the Express.
::::'''Himeko:''' They chose to work for the Express as a way to say thanks for saving their lives and pay off their rescue-related expenses.
::::'''Himeko:''' How about that? Is that good enough to satisfy your curiosities?
::::'''Himeko:''' Well, satisfied or not, you can ask Welt if you have any more questions. If you'll excuse me, (Trailblazer), I have to get on my work now.
:;(Subsequent interactions)
:::'''Himeko:''' You can go and chat with Welt if he has the time...
;(Otherwise, if {{cx}}<!--SubMission Finish: 101000205-->, {{cx}}<!--SubMission not Finish: 101100201-->, and {{cx}}<!--performance 599000102 has been seen-->)
::'''Himeko:''' Oh, back so soon?
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} We narrowly averted disaster, and now we're home.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} We almost didn't make it back...
::'''Himeko:''' Hah, it seems this world is a dangerous place, too. Ever since the Astral Express embarked on this journey, every world contaminated by the Stellaron has been problematic.
::'''Himeko:''' Before the three of you boarded the Express, Welt, I... and someone else were adventuring together. It was the same back then as well &mdash; we would slowly trailblaze new worlds, find the Stellaron, and clear a path...
::'''Himeko:''' No matter what world we were on, some difficulties remain constant &mdash; misunderstandings caused by communication, enmity caused by cultural differences, and enemies with malicious intentions. But there is always something new.
::'''Himeko:''' Keep up the good work, (Trailblazer).
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} You've never mentioned these things before...
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I want to hear about your past...
::'''Himeko:''' You've still got work to do. As for me, I've got to maintain the Express while it is parked.
::'''Himeko:''' We can take a long break after we're done with this world. Come find me if you're still interested then.
;(Otherwise, if {{cx}}<!--SubMission not Finish: 100050304--> and {{cx}}<!--SubMission Finish: 100050201-->)
::'''Himeko:''' What's wrong? You look like you were about to say something.
::'''Himeko:''' Oh, I think I know what you were going to ask. You've come to the right person.
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} About the Express...
:::'''Himeko:''' Ohh, you want to know more about the Express? I'm glad. After all, it's an important companion of ours.
:::{{Диалог|Разговор}} About the history of the Express...
::::'''Himeko:''' The Astral Express was a tool created by Akivili the Trailblaze, who used it to transport THEMSELF and the Nameless across the galaxy. It is rumored that there are other vehicles like it, but the Express has no such records.
::::'''Himeko:''' When I found the Express, its memory had been severely damaged, with much of its valuable information lost. All I know is that the Express is an Aspect of Creation built by Akivili themself, and used to travel the cosmos.
::::'''Himeko:''' As for how it was built and how it was damaged, I do not have an answer.
:::;(Return to previous option selection)
:::{{Диалог|Разговор}} About where the Express is headed...
::::'''Himeko:''' The Express is traveling on a route that the Trailblaze once embarked on. The names of some destinations have been lost, but the first and final stops were both at Pegana &mdash; Akivili's home world.
::::'''Himeko:''' We speculate the Astral Express started its journey from Pegana, stopping at each destination along the way before returning there for its next journey. However, the appearance of the Stellarons has caused a delay at each stop.
:::;(Return to previous option selection)
:::{{Диалог|Разговор}} About the Express' source of power...
::::'''Himeko:''' There is a legend in the galaxy: The heart of Akivili themself lies in the core of the Astral Express, providing it with the power to travel between worlds. But I found no evidence of that aboard the Express.
::::'''Himeko:''' Besides, the Express existed before the Trailblaze fell. There's no way they could have had two hearts, right? However, it is likely that the Express possesses some sort of mechanism to transfer power from the Trailblaze.
::::'''Himeko:''' It wouldn't be possible with a normal Pathstrider.
:::;(Return to previous option selection)
:::{{Диалог|Разговор}} About Akivili...
::::'''Himeko:''' The fallen Aeon, deceased Trailblaze &mdash; THEIR passing is still a mystery, but of all the known Aeons, Akivili was the closest to mankind.
::::'''Himeko:''' In the databank aboard the Express, it is recorded that THEY walked among the mortals &mdash; adventuring, fighting, and celebrating with THEM. Although THEY were an Aeon restrained by the "Primum Mobile," Akivili enjoyed a freedom similar to us mortals.
::::'''Himeko:''' THEY were different from most... But THEIR passing came so suddenly that it was thought THEY were killed by another Aeon. I don't believe that to be the case.
:::;(Return to previous option selection)
:::{{Диалог|Возврат}} I have another question...
::::{{Диалог|Разговор}} About the galaxy...
:::::'''Himeko:''' The galaxy is endlessly vast. I wouldn't know where to begin, especially if you ask me that so suddenly...
:::::{{Диалог|Разговор}} About its nature...
::::::'''Himeko:''' I've been to many different worlds, yet I still know very little about the galaxy, simply because it's too vast. As for its nature, there are a few theories that I can share with you.
::::::'''Himeko:''' The most popular is probably the Cosmos Tree theory, proposed by Zandar, Emanator of Erudition and the first member of the Genius Society. He compared the galaxy to an enormous imaginary tree, with its leaves being individual universes.
::::::'''Himeko:''' Therefore, only Aeons, who draw their energy from the imaginary, and Emanators, who are blessed by Aeons, can travel through the spaces filled with imaginary energy. That's why planets where civilizations exist are so similar.
::::::'''Himeko:''' However, the theory has its flaws. Elias Salas, the 56th member of the Genius Society, invented remote detection, disproving that the imaginary is unique. This shook the foundation of the "Cosmos Tree" theory.
::::::'''Himeko:''' There are other theories as well: The "Stretching" theory, the "Heat Torch" theory, and the "Parallel Imaging" theory... The Riddlers claim the galaxy is just a dream and IX's followers seem to like that claim.
:::::;(Return to previous option selection)
:::::{{Диалог|Разговор}} About the Aeons...
::::::'''Himeko:''' Aeons are the most mysterious beings in the galaxy. All we know is that THEY ascended from the form of intelligent beings. As for the how and why, even the geniuses over at the Genius Society haven't the slightest clue.
::::::'''Himeko:''' Upon ascending to Aeon-hood, that being gains power over the Paths, free to choose the allocation of imaginary energy however THEY wish, while suffering the restrictions of the "Primum Mobile."
::::::'''Himeko:''' The Aeon of Destruction seeks only to destroy the universe, while the Aeon of Erudition wants to find the answer for all that exists. Meanwhile, the Aeon of Preservation continues to forge walls, and the Aeon of Enigmata devotes themself to obscuring all that is known...
::::::'''Himeko:''' A cloud of mystery shrouds the Aeons. I heard Madam Herta recruited a team to try and solve the mysteries about THEM.
:::::;(Return to previous option selection)
:::::{{Диалог|Разговор}} About the factions...
::::::'''Himeko:''' Compared to the Aeons, the factions are much easier to understand. Mortals with the same objective gather together to practice their understanding of Aeons and the Paths.
::::::'''Himeko:''' Many Aeons are unreachable, but the factions are close to us. After Akivili trailblazed across the galaxy, people became aware of the existence of other worlds. Gradually, more people started trying to use the power of the Aeons to travel between worlds.
::::::'''Himeko:''' The Interastral Peace Corporation is a good example: They worship Qlipoth, the Aeon of Preservation, but somehow became the largest economic entity in the galaxy;
::::::'''Himeko:''' Another example is the Genius Society: There is no shortage of eccentrics like Madam Herta who dedicate themselves to scientific research under the protection of the Erudition.
::::::'''Himeko:''' These factions possess the same power as us to voyage between worlds. It would be hard to travel through the galaxy without them.
:::::;(Return to previous option selection)
:::::{{Диалог|Разговор}} About the Paths...
::::::'''Himeko:''' The birth of an Aeon gives rise to a Path. The nature of the Paths remains a mystery, leaving us to draw an analogy in a way that mortals can understand: It's a philosophical concept of sorts.
::::::'''Himeko:''' A person is considered to be on a Path when their will overlaps with that Path. If the person has a strong enough will, they can draw power from that Path. Those who can do so are called Pathstriders.
::::::'''Himeko:''' Pathstriders possess extraordinary power, but are still insignificant compared to the Aeons, like a drop of water in a vast ocean. Sometimes, Aeons will bestow a mortal with their power, making them an "Emanator" of that Aeon.
::::::'''Himeko:''' I should mention that once a Path is open, it cannot be closed, even with the fall of its Aeon. That is how we are still able to travel across the stars, despite Akivili's passing.
:::::;(Return to previous option selection)
::::;(Return to previous option selection)
::::{{Диалог|Разговор}} About Trailblaze...
:::::'''Himeko:''' "Trailblaze" is our mission and the source of strength that powers the Express to travel across the galaxy.
:::::{{Диалог|Разговор}} About Exploration...
::::::'''Himeko:''' Explore the unknown world to continue our journey ahead.
:::::;(Return to previous option selection)
:::::{{Диалог|Разговор}} About Understanding...
::::::'''Himeko:''' Understand the local culture and immerse ourselves within it.
:::::;(Return to previous option selection)
:::::{{Диалог|Разговор}} About Establishing...
::::::'''Himeko:''' Establish a connection with the new world &mdash; rejoice with it and share in its fears.
:::::;(Return to previous option selection)
:::::{{Диалог|Разговор}} About Connection...
::::::'''Himeko:''' Connect worlds together, carving an endless path.
:::::;(Return to previous option selection)
::::;(Return to previous option selection)
::::{{Диалог|Выход}} I don't have any more questions.
